                    "review_markdown":  "The added widget test can fail based on the runner locale, and the persisted-category test does not validate the compatibility contract it claims to protect.\n\nFull review comments:\n\n- [P2] Pin the widget-test locale before asserting English text ??C:\\actions-runner\\_work\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo_trunk\\test\\view\\common_widget\\new_tag_widget_test.dart:19-19\n  On a host whose platform locale resolves to German, `MaterialApp` selects the generated `general_new_tag_text` value `\"Neu\"`, so this `find.text(\u0027NEW\u0027)` lookup throws and makes the test environment-dependent. Set `locale: const Locale(\u0027en\u0027)` or obtain the expected value from `S.of(...)` before asserting it.\n\n- [P2] Assert the persisted category strings explicitly ??C:\\actions-runner\\_work\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo_trunk\\test\\model\\color_palette\\magic_template_color_palette_category_test.dart:8-10\n  This round-trip is self-referential: changing `toString()` from (for example) `\"monochrome\"` to `\"mono\"` and leaving `fromString()` tied to it will still pass, even though existing persisted/CMS values can no longer deserialize. Assert the fixed persisted strings (and their expected enum values) directly so the stated compatibility contract is actually protected.\n"
